---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
const title = 'Install bob';
const subtitle = 'The full walk. Install, invoke, all seven steps, paced for reading.';
---
<Base title={title} description={subtitle}>
  <article class="etude-page">
    <header class="etude-head">
      <p class="etude-kicker">Etude · The anti-cascader</p>
      <h1 class="etude-title">{title}</h1>
      <p class="etude-relief">{subtitle}</p>
      <nav class="etude-nav">
        <a href="/etudes/anti-cascader/">← anti-cascader etudes</a>
        <span class="etude-nav-sep">·</span>
        <a href="/puzzles/bob-the-fixer-as-anti-cascader/">essay</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <section class="etude-intro">
      <p>The team installs bob, invokes <code>/migrate-spring-boot-3</code>, and walks all seven steps of the Spring Boot 2.7 → 3 migration. Each step shows the explanation prose verbatim, runs the codemod or gate, prints a real diff against the bundled fixture, then walks the human loop: <strong>understand the change → review what to look for in the PR → wait for CI gates green → merge → next step.</strong> That loop is the etude's contribution — each step is small enough that a human can hold all of it in their head while it lands.</p>
      <p>Press play. Read the explanations. Watch the review shape repeat.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="etude-stage">
      <div class="etude-card">
        <p class="etude-step">Team's terminal · Spring Boot 2.7 repo</p>

        <ol class="step-bar" id="step-bar" aria-label="migration steps">
          <li data-step="install" class="step-pending">install</li>
          <li data-step="1" class="step-pending">1</li>
          <li data-step="2" class="step-pending">2</li>
          <li data-step="3" class="step-pending">3</li>
          <li data-step="4" class="step-pending">4</li>
          <li data-step="5" class="step-pending">5</li>
          <li data-step="6" class="step-pending">6</li>
          <li data-step="7" class="step-pending">7</li>
        </ol>

        <div class="term" id="term">
          <div class="term-chrome">
            <span class="term-dot term-dot-r"></span>
            <span class="term-dot term-dot-y"></span>
            <span class="term-dot term-dot-g"></span>
            <span class="term-title">~/svc/orders-api · main</span>
          </div>
          <div class="term-body" id="term-body" aria-live="polite"></div>
        </div>

        <div class="controls">
          <button type="button" id="play" class="etude-next">Play</button>
          <button type="button" id="reset" class="etude-ghost" disabled>Reset</button>
          <label class="speed">
            <span class="speed-label">Speed</span>
            <select id="speed">
              <option value="1" selected>1x</option>
              <option value="2">2x</option>
              <option value="4">4x</option>
            </select>
          </label>
        </div>

        <div id="banner" class="banner" aria-live="polite"></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="etude-failure">
      <h2 class="etude-failure-title">What happened</h2>
      <p>The team typed two commands. Bob walked all seven steps in sequence — a precheck gate, four deterministic codemods, one hybrid step, and a postcheck gate — pausing on each to print the publisher-authored explanation <em>before</em> running it, then showing the diff, then opening a draft PR with a <code>Bob-Step:</code> trailer. <strong>Seven small reviewable PRs land in the team's queue.</strong></p>
      <p>State lives in <code>git log</code>. The next invocation re-derives the same step pointer from the trailers on main. Pause for a quarter, hand to a colleague, run on a fresh clone — same answer.</p>
      <p>The platform team that authored the migration never opened the PR. They wrote the codemods and the explanations and shipped it as a skill. The team pulled.</p>
    </section>

    <footer class="etude-coda">
      <p>Single-shot would have been one 700-line PR. Choreographed is seven small PRs, each one with the explanation in front of it. The team reads each one.</p>
    </footer>
  </article>
</Base>

<script is:inline>
  // A scripted terminal transcript. Each frame is either a typed line, a printed
  // line, or a multi-line block. The animation paces through the choreography
  // — install, invoke, explain, run, diff, PR, stop — at the user's chosen speed.

  const FRAMES = [
    // ── 1. Install bob ────────────────────────────────────────────
    { kind: 'step', id: 'install' },
    { kind: 'prompt', text: '~ %' },
    { kind: 'type', text: 'claude' },
    { kind: 'enter' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: 'Claude Code · session started' },
    { kind: 'gap' },

    { kind: 'cc-prompt' },
    { kind: 'type', text: '/plugin marketplace add https://raw.githubusercontent.com/parrik/bob-the-fixer/main/.claude-plugin/marketplace.json' },
    { kind: 'enter' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: 'added marketplace: bob-the-fixer' },
    { kind: 'gap' },

    { kind: 'cc-prompt' },
    { kind: 'type', text: '/plugin install bob-the-fixer' },
    { kind: 'enter' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: 'installed: bob-the-fixer (4 skills)' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '  /migrate-spring-boot-3' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '  /migrate-junit-4-to-5' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '  /migrate-jest-to-vitest' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '  /adopt-structured-logging' },
    { kind: 'gap' },

    // ── 2. Invoke the migration ───────────────────────────────────
    { kind: 'cc-prompt' },
    { kind: 'type', text: '/migrate-spring-boot-3' },
    { kind: 'enter' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: 'claude code dispatches to bob:' },
    { kind: 'gap' },
    { kind: 'prompt', text: '~/svc/orders-api %' },
    { kind: 'type', text: 'bash bob-simulator.sh . migrate-spring-boot-3' },
    { kind: 'enter' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ scanning git log on main for Bob-Step: trailers' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ found 0 step(s) done; advancing to step 01' },
    { kind: 'gap' },

    // ── 3. Step 01 · precheck (gate) ──────────────────────────────
    { kind: 'step', id: '1' },
    { kind: 'block', cls: 'term-explain', lines: [
      '┌─ step 01 · pre-flight: is this repo ready? ───────────',
      '│',
      '│ Bails if the repo can\'t be migrated cleanly. Checks:',
      '│  - on Spring Boot 2.7+ (older = needs intermediate hop)',
      '│  - no in-flight branches that would conflict',
      '│  - tests currently green on main',
      '│  - has a CI pipeline we can wait on',
      '│',
      '│ If any check fails, surface a runbook entry — don\'t',
      '│ proceed.',
      '└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────',
    ]},
    { kind: 'gap-long' },

    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ running steps/01-precheck/check.sh' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '  PASS: Spring Boot 2.7.18' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '  PASS: working tree clean' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '  PASS: tests currently green' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '  PASS: CI configured' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '  All prechecks passed. Ready to migrate.' },
    { kind: 'gap' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ recording empty commit: Bob-Step: migrate-spring-boot-3/01-precheck' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '✓ precheck passed; nothing to merge yet (gate step — no PR opens)' },
    { kind: 'gap-long' },

    // ── 4. Step 02 · jakarta imports (codemod) ────────────────────
    { kind: 'step', id: '2' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ scanning git log on main for Bob-Step: trailers' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ found 1 step(s) done; advancing to step 02' },
    { kind: 'gap' },

    { kind: 'block', cls: 'term-explain', lines: [
      '┌─ step 02 · rename javax.* → jakarta.* ─────────────────',
      '│',
      '│ Spring Boot 3 moved off the javax.* namespace to',
      '│ jakarta.* Mechanical, byte-deterministic. Touches',
      '│ imports + fully-qualified references. Common subset:',
      '│   javax.persistence.*  → jakarta.persistence.*',
      '│   javax.servlet.*      → jakarta.servlet.*',
      '│   javax.validation.*   → jakarta.validation.*',
      '│   javax.annotation.*   → jakarta.annotation.*',
      '│',
      '│ This is by far the largest diff but also the safest —',
      '│ the AST pattern is unambiguous. Expect 100s-1000s of',
      '│ import lines touched.',
      '└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────',
    ]},
    { kind: 'gap-long' },

    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ running steps/02-jakarta-imports/transform.ts' },
    { kind: 'progress', total: 6 },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ 6 files changed · +18 −18' },
    { kind: 'gap' },

    { kind: 'block', cls: 'term-diff', lines: [
      'src/main/java/com/example/demo/User.java',
      '-import javax.persistence.Entity;',
      '-import javax.persistence.GeneratedValue;',
      '-import javax.persistence.Id;',
      '-import javax.validation.constraints.Email;',
      '+import jakarta.persistence.Entity;',
      '+import jakarta.persistence.GeneratedValue;',
      '+import jakarta.persistence.Id;',
      '+import jakarta.validation.constraints.Email;',
      '',
      'src/main/java/com/example/demo/controller/OrderController.java',
      '-import javax.servlet.http.HttpServletRequest;',
      '-import javax.validation.Valid;',
      '+import jakarta.servlet.http.HttpServletRequest;',
      '+import jakarta.validation.Valid;',
    ]},
    { kind: 'gap' },

    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ checkpoint: ./mvnw compile && ./mvnw test' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '  BUILD SUCCESS · tests pass' },
    { kind: 'gap' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ creating branch: bob/migrate-spring-boot-3/02-jakarta-imports' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ committing with Bob-Step: migrate-spring-boot-3/02-jakarta-imports' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ opening draft PR #1: "chore(migration): step 02 — javax→jakarta imports"' },
    { kind: 'gap-long' },

    { kind: 'block', cls: 'term-review', lines: [
      '┌─ PR review · step 02 ─────────────────────────────────',
      '│ what this PR does:',
      '│   rename javax.* → jakarta.* across imports + FQ refs',
      '│',
      '│ what to look at in review:',
      '│   • skim the javax.* → jakarta.* rewrites in changed',
      '│     files; the AST pattern is unambiguous but eyeball',
      '│     anyway',
      '│   • check for reflection-based class strings still',
      '│     referencing "javax.persistence.*" — codemod doesn\'t',
      '│     touch string literals',
      '│   • confirm pom.xml / build files were NOT touched —',
      '│     the SB version bump lives in step 04',
      '│   • confirm tests still compile: ./mvnw compile',
      '└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────',
    ]},
    { kind: 'gap-long' },

    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ CI · build .................. ✓ pass' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ CI · tests .................. ✓ pass' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ CI · lint ................... ✓ pass' },
    { kind: 'gap' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ team approves & merges PR #1' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ commit on main: a3f1c2d · Bob-Step: migrate-spring-boot-3/02-jakarta-imports' },
    { kind: 'gap-long' },

    // ── 5. Step 03 · properties (codemod) ─────────────────────────
    { kind: 'step', id: '3' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ scanning git log on main for Bob-Step: trailers' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ found 2 step(s) done; advancing to step 03' },
    { kind: 'gap' },

    { kind: 'block', cls: 'term-explain', lines: [
      '┌─ step 03 · rewrite application.{yml,properties} keys ──',
      '│',
      '│ Spring Boot 3 renamed several config keys. Mechanical:',
      '│   spring.redis.*           → spring.data.redis.*',
      '│   spring.elasticsearch.*   → spring.elasticsearch.uris',
      '│   management.metrics.export → management.{specific',
      '│                                 exporter}.metrics.export',
      '│',
      '│ Codemod uses YAML / properties parsers (not regex) so',
      '│ comments and ordering are preserved.',
      '└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────',
    ]},
    { kind: 'gap-long' },

    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ running steps/03-properties/transform.ts' },
    { kind: 'progress', total: 3 },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ 3 files changed · +14 −14' },
    { kind: 'gap' },

    { kind: 'block', cls: 'term-diff', lines: [
      'src/main/resources/application.properties',
      '-spring.jpa.hibernate.use-new-id-generator-mappings=true',
      '-spring.datasource.initialization-mode=always',
      '-spring.datasource.schema=classpath:schema.sql',
      '-spring.datasource.data=classpath:data.sql',
      '-server.error.include-stacktrace=on_trace_param',
      '-spring.profiles=integration',
      '-management.metrics.export.wavefront.api-token=REPLACE_ME',
      '+spring.sql.init.mode=always',
      '+spring.sql.init.schema-locations=classpath:schema.sql',
      '+spring.sql.init.data-locations=classpath:data.sql',
      '+server.error.include-stacktrace=on_param',
      '+spring.config.activate.on-profile=integration',
      '+management.wavefront.metrics.export.api-token=REPLACE_ME',
    ]},
    { kind: 'gap' },

    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ checkpoint: ./mvnw compile' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '  BUILD SUCCESS' },
    { kind: 'gap' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ creating branch: bob/migrate-spring-boot-3/03-properties' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ committing with Bob-Step: migrate-spring-boot-3/03-properties' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ opening draft PR #2: "chore(migration): step 03 — application property renames"' },
    { kind: 'gap-long' },

    { kind: 'block', cls: 'term-review', lines: [
      '┌─ PR review · step 03 ─────────────────────────────────',
      '│ what this PR does:',
      '│   rewrite renamed config keys in application.{yml,',
      '│   properties} for SB3',
      '│',
      '│ what to look at in review:',
      '│   • eyeball the renamed keys against the SB3 release',
      '│     notes — small surface, easy to scan',
      '│   • check application-{dev,staging,prod}.yml for',
      '│     environment overrides that might use the old key',
      '│     names — codemod scans every yml/properties file but',
      '│     review confirms',
      '│   • flag if your project depends on properties-file',
      '│     comments — YAML round-trip preserves them, but the',
      '│     properties parser may drop trailing comments',
      '└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────',
    ]},
    { kind: 'gap-long' },

    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ CI · build .................. ✓ pass' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ CI · tests .................. ✓ pass' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ CI · lint ................... ✓ pass' },
    { kind: 'gap' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ team approves & merges PR #2' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ commit on main: 4e92b18 · Bob-Step: migrate-spring-boot-3/03-properties' },
    { kind: 'gap-long' },

    // ── 6. Step 04 · build bumps (codemod) ────────────────────────
    { kind: 'step', id: '4' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ scanning git log on main for Bob-Step: trailers' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ found 3 step(s) done; advancing to step 04' },
    { kind: 'gap' },

    { kind: 'block', cls: 'term-explain', lines: [
      '┌─ step 04 · bump Spring Boot + Java in build files ─────',
      '│',
      '│ Single bump in pom.xml or build.gradle:',
      '│   spring-boot version  → 3.2.x (latest patch)',
      '│   java.version         → 17 (or 21)',
      '│   + plugin compatibility bumps (jib,',
      '│     spring-boot-maven-plugin)',
      '└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────',
    ]},
    { kind: 'gap-long' },

    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ running steps/04-build-bumps/transform.ts' },
    { kind: 'progress', total: 1 },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ 1 file changed · +4 −4' },
    { kind: 'gap' },

    { kind: 'block', cls: 'term-diff', lines: [
      'pom.xml',
      '-        <version>2.7.18</version>',
      '+        <version>3.3.5</version>',
      '',
      '-        <java.version>11</java.version>',
      '+        <java.version>17</java.version>',
      '',
      '-            <groupId>mysql</groupId>',
      '-            <artifactId>mysql-connector-java</artifactId>',
      '+            <groupId>com.mysql</groupId>',
      '+            <artifactId>mysql-connector-j</artifactId>',
    ]},
    { kind: 'gap' },

    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ checkpoint: ./mvnw dependency:tree -DoutputType=text' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '  jakarta.* resolves cleanly · no surprise transitives' },
    { kind: 'gap' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ creating branch: bob/migrate-spring-boot-3/04-build-bumps' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ committing with Bob-Step: migrate-spring-boot-3/04-build-bumps' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ opening draft PR #3: "chore(migration): step 04 — bump Spring Boot 3.3.5 + Java 17"' },
    { kind: 'gap-long' },

    { kind: 'block', cls: 'term-review', lines: [
      '┌─ PR review · step 04 ─────────────────────────────────',
      '│ what this PR does:',
      '│   bump spring-boot to 3.x and java.version to 17 in',
      '│   build files',
      '│',
      '│ what to look at in review:',
      '│   • confirm the SB version landed at 3.x and Java at 17',
      '│     (or 21 if your fleet is there)',
      '│   • run ./mvnw dependency:tree | grep CONFLICT — flag',
      '│     any transitive dep that didn\'t resolve cleanly',
      '│   • confirm test runner versions are still compatible',
      '│     (JUnit 5, Mockito) — SB3 nudges minimum versions',
      '│   • check plugin compatibility (jib, spring-boot-maven-',
      '│     plugin) — codemod bumps them but eyeball',
      '└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────',
    ]},
    { kind: 'gap-long' },

    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ CI · build .................. ✓ pass' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ CI · tests .................. ✓ pass' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ CI · lint ................... ✓ pass' },
    { kind: 'gap' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ team approves & merges PR #3' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ commit on main: 7d20a4f · Bob-Step: migrate-spring-boot-3/04-build-bumps' },
    { kind: 'gap-long' },

    // ── 7. Step 05 · deprecated APIs (codemod) ────────────────────
    { kind: 'step', id: '5' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ scanning git log on main for Bob-Step: trailers' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ found 4 step(s) done; advancing to step 05' },
    { kind: 'gap' },

    { kind: 'block', cls: 'term-explain', lines: [
      '┌─ step 05 · rewrite deprecated APIs removed in SB3 ─────',
      '│',
      '│ Spring Boot 3 removed APIs that were deprecated in',
      '│ 2.x. Mechanical rewrites for the common ones:',
      '│   WebSecurityConfigurerAdapter → SecurityFilterChain bean',
      '│   antMatchers / mvcMatchers    → requestMatchers',
      '│   @MockBean (in tests)         → unchanged but check',
      '│                                  Mockito ver',
      '│   ResponseEntityExceptionHandler → updated method',
      '│                                    signatures',
      '│',
      '│ Some have no clean codemod (security config can be',
      '│ hand-rolled in ways the pattern misses). Those get',
      '│ flagged for step 06.',
      '└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────',
    ]},
    { kind: 'gap-long' },

    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ running steps/05-deprecated-apis/transform.ts' },
    { kind: 'progress', total: 2 },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ 1 file changed · +9 −5 · 0 sites flagged for step 06' },
    { kind: 'gap' },

    { kind: 'block', cls: 'term-diff', lines: [
      'src/main/java/com/example/demo/SecurityConfig.java',
      '-import org.springframework.security.config.annotation.web.configuration.WebSecurityConfigurerAdapter;',
      '+import org.springframework.context.annotation.Bean;',
      '+import org.springframework.security.web.SecurityFilterChain;',
      '',
      '-public class SecurityConfig extends WebSecurityConfigurerAdapter {',
      '-    @Override',
      '-    protected void configure(HttpSecurity http) throws Exception {',
      '+public class SecurityConfig {',
      '+    @Bean',
      '+    SecurityFilterChain securityFilterChain(HttpSecurity http) throws Exception {',
      '         http',
      '-            .authorizeRequests()',
      '-                .antMatchers("/users/me").authenticated()',
      '-                .antMatchers("/users/**").permitAll()',
      '+            .authorizeHttpRequests()',
      '+                .requestMatchers("/users/me").authenticated()',
      '+                .requestMatchers("/users/**").permitAll()',
      '+        return http.build();',
      '     }',
      ' }',
    ]},
    { kind: 'gap' },

    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ checkpoint: ./mvnw compile' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '  BUILD SUCCESS' },
    { kind: 'gap' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ creating branch: bob/migrate-spring-boot-3/05-deprecated-apis' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ committing with Bob-Step: migrate-spring-boot-3/05-deprecated-apis' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ opening draft PR #4: "chore(migration): step 05 — SecurityFilterChain + requestMatchers"' },
    { kind: 'gap-long' },

    { kind: 'block', cls: 'term-review', lines: [
      '┌─ PR review · step 05 ─────────────────────────────────',
      '│ what this PR does:',
      '│   rewrite WebSecurityConfigurerAdapter → SecurityFilter-',
      '│   Chain bean and antMatchers → requestMatchers',
      '│',
      '│ what to look at in review:',
      '│   • read the SecurityFilterChain bean carefully — the',
      '│     chain DSL needs to be preserved 1:1; this is the',
      '│     highest-blast-radius rewrite in the migration',
      '│   • check any flag-only comments bob left — sites the',
      '│     codemod couldn\'t rewrite mechanically; a human',
      '│     handles those by hand in a follow-up',
      '│   • confirm no security regressions: every endpoint',
      '│     that required auth before still does (read the',
      '│     before/after of authorizeRequests → authorize-',
      '│     HttpRequests)',
      '└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────',
    ]},
    { kind: 'gap-long' },

    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ CI · build .................. ✓ pass' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ CI · tests .................. ✓ pass' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ CI · lint ................... ✓ pass' },
    { kind: 'gap' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ team approves & merges PR #4' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ commit on main: 1b5e83a · Bob-Step: migrate-spring-boot-3/05-deprecated-apis' },
    { kind: 'gap-long' },

    // ── 8. Step 06 · hibernate queries (hybrid, no-op on this fixture) ─
    { kind: 'step', id: '6' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ scanning git log on main for Bob-Step: trailers' },
    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ found 5 step(s) done; advancing to step 06' },
    { kind: 'gap' },

    { kind: 'block', cls: 'term-explain', lines: [
      '┌─ step 06 · Hibernate 6 query rewrites (LLM-assisted) ──',
      '│',
      '│ Spring Boot 3 ships with Hibernate 6. HB6 changed',
      '│ several HQL/JPQL semantics with no clean mechanical',
      '│ fix. The flagger looks for five patterns; a hybrid LLM',
      '│ step proposes per-site rewrites for human approval.',
      '│',
      '│ Two passes:',
      '│  (a) AST scan: locate every @Query, @NamedQuery, and',
      '│      HQL string against the five HB6 patterns.',
      '│  (b) For each match: LLM proposes a rewrite. The',
      '│      HUMAN approves each one — no silent rewrites.',
      '│',
      '│ Why a separate step: rewrites are non-deterministic.',
      '│ Team should review each individually, not as one PR.',
      '└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────',
    ]},
    { kind: 'gap-long' },

    { kind: 'echo', text: '→ running steps/06-hibernate-queries/flag-pattern.ts' },
